<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 12:50:33 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>Spain's Sanchez says no 'solid proof' that Morocco planned Ceuta crisis</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-spain-s-sanchez-says-no-solid-proof-that-morocco-planned-ceuta-crisis</link><description>
Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez has told lawmakers that there is no evidence the Ceuta migrant crisis was orchestrated by Morocco's government. His remarks come a day after tens of thousands of people took part in protests across the country to criticize his handling of the migrant influx. He acknowledged that Ceuta was both a humanitarian crisis and an administrative challenge. But he rejected the findings of a police report that seemed to lay blame on Morocco. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris reports from Madrid, Spain.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1e5bde64-8ce1-11f1-a75a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-31T112414Z-409645030-RC2ZOMA4UF9K-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CEUTA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1e5bde64-8ce1-11f1-a75a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-31T112414Z-409645030-RC2ZOMA4UF9K-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CEUTA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6a2d278a-a785-11f1-b12a-3bc92fe369a2</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 11:58:47 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Senegalese consumers rally online against rising cost of living</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-senegalese-consumers-rally-online-against-rising-cost-of-living</link><description>
In Senegal, the price of a kilogram of meat has risen from 3,800 to 5,500 CFA francs in just a few months, while the price of onions has doubled. Fuel, transportation, rent… No sector has been spared by the surge in prices. Senegalese consumers who are frustrated by the rising cost of living in Dakar have launched a new hashtag: #30DaysForTheRightPrice. The organisers of this widely shared digital campaign want to alert the authorities to the social consequences of the situation, particularly for the most vulnerable households. FRANCE 24's team on the ground reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d161c5f6-a784-11f1-a4cb-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260902-215341-215537-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d161c5f6-a784-11f1-a4cb-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260902-215341-215537-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d7314bdc-a784-11f1-825d-bba181e6f0ff</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 10:53:15 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nepal: How are the hundreds of victims from the floods being identified?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-nepal-how-are-the-hundreds-of-victims-from-the-floods-being-identified</link><description>
#Nepal faces a major challenge: identifying the remains that have been found after the #flood that tore through part of the country on August 26, some of which are in an advanced state of decomposition. For #health reasons, the unidentified bodies have begun to be buried. Before each #burial, #DNA samples are taken and an identification number is assigned to each set of remains. Relatives of those reported missing can visit DNA collection centres to provide a sample. Their genetic profile can then be compared with that of the bodies found, in the hope of identifying them. FRANCE 24’s correspondents visited one such centre, set up within the #police #hospital in #Kathmandu.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/14e0b356-a784-11f1-8616-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Vignette-DNA-2.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/14e0b356-a784-11f1-8616-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Vignette-DNA-2.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">372b7b3a-a784-11f1-b089-bba181e6f0ff</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 10:52:41 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Premier League sets new transfer market record</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20260903-premier-league-sets-new-transfer-market-record</link><description>
There’s the Premier League and then there’s everyone else. The 20 Premier League sides spent more than €4 billion this summer in the transfer market, setting a new record. Manchester City broke the record for the most spent by a single club in one summer, with more than €500 million spent on new signings. That's almost as much as the 18 French Ligue 1 clubs combined (€605 million).
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ebe17c84-a755-11f1-9a57-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26235519663073.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ebe17c84-a755-11f1-9a57-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26235519663073.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">66634506-a755-11f1-8d30-f3a9d7bd2ae4</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 10:51:37 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>L'Equipe TV</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>DRC Ebola outbreak shows no signs of slowing as deaths top 3,000</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-drc-ebola-outbreak-shows-no-signs-of-slowing-as-deaths-top-3-000</link><description>
Congo’s Ebola outbreak has killed more than 3,000 people out of more than 6,100 confirmed cases, according to the latest government data from Wednesday, as the disease is spreading at an unprecedented speed, faster than efforts to track and slow it. Data from Congo’s Ministry of Health showed the outbreak has recorded 6,186 confirmed cases, including 3,007 deaths since it was declared a global health emergency in mid-May. It remains the fastest-growing outbreak of Ebola ever. FRANCE 24's Emmet Livingstone reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/206fd418-a784-11f1-8253-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260902-215150-215309-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/206fd418-a784-11f1-8253-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260902-215150-215309-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">25524506-a784-11f1-a723-3bc92fe369a2</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 10:45:36 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Press Review</category><title>Supreme Court corruption scandal rocks Brazil</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260903-supreme-court-corruption-scandal-rocks-brazil</link><description>
PRESS REVIEW – Thursday, September 3: There's outrage in Malta after a tycoon was found not guilty of masterminding the murder of high-profile investigative journalist Daphne Caruana Galizia. In Brazil, a Supreme Court justice who was pivotal in sentencing former President Jair Bolsonaro to prison is implicated in a corruption scandal of his own. Plus conservationists marvel after a mating frenzy of the endangered kakapo – a flightless, nocturnal parrot native to New Zealand.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/966db16a-a763-11f1-883c-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Anglais-2026-09-03T05-24-59-031Z.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/966db16a-a763-11f1-883c-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Anglais-2026-09-03T05-24-59-031Z.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9c900304-a763-11f1-b86d-9f70221deb09</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 10:42:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Dheepthika LAURENT</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Tunisia's top court set to rule in ‘conspiracy against the state’ case</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-tunisia-s-top-court-set-to-rule-in-conspiracy-against-the-state-case</link><description>
In Tunisia, the Court of Cassation is set to issue its final ruling in the “conspiracy against the state” case. In April 2025, 37 people – most of them prominent political figures opposed to President Kais Saied – were sentenced to prison in connection with the case. Several human rights organisations have condemned the trial as unjust and called for the release of all political detainees. The appeal represents the defendants’ last legal avenue to overturn their convictions, according to a press release from Amnesty International. But defence lawyers and the detainees’ families remain pessimistic, as FRANCE 24’s Lilia Blaise reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1905cc66-a77d-11f1-8ecf-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260902-214859-215101-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1905cc66-a77d-11f1-8ecf-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260902-214859-215101-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1e005d4e-a77d-11f1-a492-6be120fbcf4d</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 10:36:37 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Tapestry diplomacy: UK-France ties in focus as Macron and Burnham hold first talks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-tapestry-diplomacy-uk-france-ties-in-focus-as-macron-and-burnham-hold-first-talks</link><description>
The Bayeux Tapestry may have brought them together — but migrant crossings and Ukraine are likely to dominate the agenda as UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham and French President Emmanuel Macron hold their first formal talks on Thursday. The two leaders met for the first time on Wednesday evening at a preview of the tapestry’s exhibition at the British Museum, alongside King Charles III. The occasion was hailed by both sides as a symbol of improving relations between Britain and France. For more, FRANCE 24’s Stuart Norval is joined by our London correspondent Bénédicte Paviot and FRANCE 24’s International Affairs Editor Philip Turle.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0517df02-a77b-11f1-bca7-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260903-100140-101453-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0517df02-a77b-11f1-bca7-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260903-100140-101453-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">09cfd6d0-a77b-11f1-8b48-6be120fbcf4d</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 10:32:24 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>In an art gallery far, far away: George Lucas unveils art galaxy at new LA museum</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-in-an-art-gallery-far-far-away-george-lucas-unveils-art-galaxy-at-new-la-museum</link><description>
George Lucas, the legendary creator of the "Star Wars" saga, on Wednesday showcased his long-awaited Museum of Narrative Art, the culmination of nearly two decades of work and numerous obstacles. "I'm used to doing the impossible. This one almost broke my will," Lucas said as he offered reporters a first glimpse inside, ahead of the museum's official opening on September 22. Lucas, 82, has described the complex built with his wife and business partner, Mellody Hobson, as the "people's temple of art."
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3992afb4-a77b-11f1-aec7-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260903-111255-111443-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3992afb4-a77b-11f1-aec7-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260903-111255-111443-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3e83244a-a77b-11f1-a7aa-6be120fbcf4d</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 10:31:01 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Kenyan editor found safe after abduction by armed men</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-kenyan-editor-found-safe-after-abduction-by-armed-men</link><description>
An editor of one of Kenya's largest media groups was abducted by armed men and release hours later at the edge of a dam more ​than 200 ‌km away, his employer said on Wednesday. Alex Kiprotich, an associate editor at ⁠Standard Group, was taken from a car near the city of Nakuru shortly before 9:20pm on Tuesday, the company said in a statement. FRANCE 24's Bastien Renouil reports from Nairobi, Kenya.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d09759e6-a77b-11f1-9d93-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260902-214454-214636-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d09759e6-a77b-11f1-9d93-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260902-214454-214636-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d551624c-a77b-11f1-b3f8-61d24622b9c9</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 10:29:18 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>Putin's 'global battle' against US, NATO: Russia 'testing' NATO since 2022 Ukraine invasion began</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260903-putin-s-global-battle-against-us-nato-russia-testing-nato-since-2022-ukraine-invasion-began</link><description>
François Picard is pleased to welcome Anna Borshchevskaya, Senior Fellow at The Washington Institute. She interprets Russia’s reported missile support for Iran not as an isolated arms transaction, but as part of a broader geopolitical strategy in which Moscow treats Ukraine, Iran, NATO, and the United States as interconnected fronts. In her analysis, Vladimir Putin’s objective is less about pursuing direct military confrontation with Washington than about altering the strategic environment around it: strengthening actors hostile to the United States, increasing the costs of American and Israeli military action, and repeatedly probing Western thresholds for retaliation.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c224c548-a71b-11f1-bc68-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260902-180342-181121-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c224c548-a71b-11f1-bc68-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260902-180342-181121-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f52d6272-a781-11f1-b75d-3bc92fe369a2</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 10:26:42 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><title>🔴 Gloria Steinem, feminist trailblazer and award-winning journalist, dies at 92</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/culture/20260903-gloria-steinem-feminist-trailblazer-and-award-winning-journalist-dies-at-92</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">69e30136-a781-11f1-b1b6-bba181e6f0ff</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 10:24:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Culture</category><title>Gloria Steinem, feminist trailblazer and award-winning journalist, dies at 92</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/culture/20260903-gloria-steinem-feminist-trailblazer-and-award-winning-journalist-dies-at-92</link><description>
Feminist activist and journalist Gloria Steinem died on Wednesday, at the age 92, her foundation said in an Instagram post on Thursday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7619c1c8-a787-11f1-b65b-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP431130203043.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7619c1c8-a787-11f1-b65b-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP431130203043.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3ee94a6c-a781-11f1-baca-3bc92fe369a2</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 10:22:07 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7619c1c8-a787-11f1-b65b-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP431130203043.jpg">© Jacquelyn Martin, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Meloni government sets longevity record in Italy</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-meloni-government-sets-longevity-record-in-italy</link><description>
Giorgia Meloni's hard-right government has been in power for 1,413 days. She surpassed the record set by Silvio Berlusconi between 2001 and 2005, making her government Italy's longest serving uninterrupted government since World War II, after a period of intense instability. Italy has had 68 governments in the last 80 years. Giorgia Meloni and her party will celebrate the feat on Friday with a huge pre-election rally in the southern city of Bari. FRANCE 24's Seema Gupta tells more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4e304d96-8ce6-11f1-8b95-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B87T4P8.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4e304d96-8ce6-11f1-8b95-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B87T4P8.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ba705724-a778-11f1-8437-61d24622b9c9</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 10:11:05 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Norway seizes Russian ship to enforce $4.22 billion Ukrainian compensation claim</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260903-norway-seizes-russian-ship-to-enforce-4-22-billion-ukrainian-arbitration-claim</link><description>
Norway said Wednesday it had seized a Russian ship as part of a Ukrainian effort to recover $4.22 billion awarded to state energy firm Naftogaz over Russia’s seizure of its assets in Crimea in 2014. The Professor Molchanov vessel was detained off the Arctic Svalbard archipelago after a Norwegian court ordered its arrest.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b1ee5b0e-a779-11f1-a62b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26246257525164.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b1ee5b0e-a779-11f1-a62b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26246257525164.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1c3a36fe-a77a-11f1-b953-6be120fbcf4d</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 10:07:06 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b1ee5b0e-a779-11f1-a62b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26246257525164.jpg">© Mindaugas Kulbis, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>After Nepal’s devastating floods, DNA tests help identify victims</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-nepal-struggles-to-identify-the-remains-found-in-floods</link><description>
The recent flash floods in Nepal have left authorities facing a major challenge: identifying the remains that have been recovered, some of which are in an advanced state of decomposition. For health reasons, unidentified bodies have begun to be buried. Before each burial, DNA samples are taken, while relatives of people reported missing can visit DNA collection centres to provide samples of their own. Their genetic profiles can then be compared with those of the recovered remains, in the hope of identifying them. FRANCE 24’s team on the ground reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0565c404-a773-11f1-b000-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26245531226042.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0565c404-a773-11f1-b000-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26245531226042.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5a137a40-a774-11f1-b2c5-4168adfd404e</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 10:06:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Brazilian justice faces pressure for alleged links to disgraced banker</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-brazilian-justice-faces-pressure-for-alleged-links-to-disgraced-banker</link><description>
The Brazilian Supreme Court justice who sentenced former far-right president Jair Bolsonaro to 27 years in prison for attempting a coup is facing pressure to resign for alleged links to a disgraced banker and potential conflict of interest. This comes weeks ahead of the presidential election in which Bolsonaro's son, Flavio Bolsonaro, is a candidate.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/68e9ed4a-8520-11f1-bc2b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/FOTO-6.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/68e9ed4a-8520-11f1-bc2b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/FOTO-6.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4c84d53e-a776-11f1-ab34-4168adfd404e</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 09:59:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>China lambasts France’s ‘discriminatory’ fast-fashion law</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260903-china-lambasts-france-s-discriminatory-fast-fashion-law</link><description>
China on Thursday called on France to abandon a new law on ultra-fast fashion that would impose fees of up to almost €20 per garment, calling it "clearly discriminatory". The law, which targets major Asian e-commerce platforms including Shein and Temu, aims to curb the industry's environmental and local economic impacts.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3fb750fe-a774-11f1-aaf9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-10T145545Z-1507510793-RC2CQHAVLDBA-RTRMADP-3-SHEIN-IPO.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3fb750fe-a774-11f1-aaf9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-10T145545Z-1507510793-RC2CQHAVLDBA-RTRMADP-3-SHEIN-IPO.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">aeae12b8-a774-11f1-8e50-61d24622b9c9</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 09:21:51 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3fb750fe-a774-11f1-aaf9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-10T145545Z-1507510793-RC2CQHAVLDBA-RTRMADP-3-SHEIN-IPO.jpg">© Sarah Meyssonnier, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><title>🔴 No 'solid proof' Morocco planned Ceuta migrant rush, says Spanish PM Sanchez</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260903-spanish-pm-sanchez-says-no-solid-proof-morocco-planned-ceuta-migrant-rush</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">9c01174e-a771-11f1-b187-7315e0317495</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 08:32:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>No 'solid proof' Morocco planned Ceuta migrant rush, says Spanish PM Sanchez</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260903-spanish-pm-sanchez-says-no-solid-proof-morocco-planned-ceuta-migrant-rush</link><description>
Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez said Thursday there was no "solid proof" that Morocco orchestrated a migrant rush into Ceuta in July following the emergence of a police report highlighting multiple failings by Moroccan security forces.
